<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Area enclosed by a curve and the x-axis</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The curve \(y = {@fx@}\) crosses the \(x\)-axis at two points.</p><p>(a) Find the smaller \(x\)-coordinate.</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the larger \(x\)-coordinate.</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the exact area enclosed by the curve and the \(x\)-axis.</p><div>Area \(=\) [[input:ans3]] square units [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Sketch first. The curve is an upside-down parabola, above the \(x\)-axis between its two intercepts, so the enclosed area is the integral between them.</p><p>(a), (b) \({@fx@} = {@-mm*(x-pp)*(x-qq)@}\), so \(y = 0\) when \(x = {@pp@}\) or \(x = {@qq@}\).</p><p>(c) \[\int_{ {@pp@} }^{ {@qq@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx = \left[{@Fx@}\right]_{ {@pp@} }^{ {@qq@} } = {@Fq@} - \left({@Fp@}\right) = {@A@}\]</p><p>The area is \({@A@}\) square units.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: area enclosed by a parabola and the axis. [m, p, q]: y = m(x - p)(q - x). Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 11, Exercise C questions 7 to 9. */
L: [[6,1,5],[3,2,4],[2,3,6],[3,-1,3],[1,3,9],[6,-2,1],[6,1,3],[3,3,7],[6,2,6],[6,2,5]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
mm: L[ix][1]; pp: L[ix][2]; qq: L[ix][3];
fx: expand(mm*(x-pp)*(qq-x));
Fx: integrate(fx,x);
A: subst(x=qq,Fx)-subst(x=pp,Fx);
/* diagnostics */
negA: -A;
from0: subst(x=qq,Fx)-subst(x=0,Fx);
wrongroots: subst(x=-pp,Fx)-subst(x=-qq,Fx);
Fq: subst(x=qq,Fx); Fp: subst(x=pp,Fx);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, m={@mm@}, p={@pp@}, q={@qq@}, area={@A@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Integration: area enclosed by a curve and the x-axis</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.2: Find where a quadratic curve crosses the x-axis and the exact area it encloses with the axis.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Exercise C, Questions 7 to 9 in Chapter 11 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new curves given in expanded form, so the intercepts must be found first.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
